# LUNARA — environment
#
# Copy to `.env.local` for development. On Vercel these come from the project's
# environment variables; `vercel env pull --yes` writes them into `.env.local`.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The one flag that runs the whole site.
#
# "waitlist" (default) or "store". Resolved server-side on every request. It changes only
# the commerce surfaces — nav action, announcement bar, home block 3, product buy panel,
# /bag, shop CTAs and the FAQ ordering group.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
SITE_MODE=waitlist

# Lets a reviewer flip modes on a deployment via /preview/store and /preview/waitlist.
# Off in production unless set to 1. Never enable it on the live site.
# LUNARA_ALLOW_MODE_PREVIEW=0

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Waitlist storage — Neon Postgres, provisioned through the Vercel Marketplace.
#
# Without this the waitlist falls back to a local JSON file under .data/, which works in
# `next dev` but loses signups on a read-only serverless filesystem.
#
# Apply src/lib/waitlist/schema.sql once against the database before first use.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://...

# The Founding 500 counter is seeded so the progress bar reflects the real list rather than
# starting from zero on a fresh database. Set to 0 to show only stored signups.
# WAITLIST_SEED_COUNT=417

# Absolute URL for canonical links and Open Graph metadata.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://lunara.co
